  "hero": {
    "filename": "Manhattan smoke plume on September 11, 2001 from International Space Station (Expedition 3 crew).jpg",
    "title": "File:Manhattan smoke plume on September 11, 2001 from International Space Station (Expedition 3 crew).jpg",
    "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6b/Manhattan_smoke_plume_on_September_11%2C_2001_from_International_Space_Station_%28Expedition_3_crew%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
    "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manhattan_smoke_plume_on_September_11,_2001_from_International_Space_Station_(Expedition_3_crew).jpg",
    "width": 3060,
    "height": 2033,
    "mime": "image/jpeg",
    "license": "Public domain",
    "artist": "NASA",
    "credit": "NASA Image of the Day #1171 and #1446:\n\n1171 description high resolution image\n1446 description high resolution image\nNASA Human Spaceflight: description high resolution image",
    "source": "Manhattan smoke plume on September 11, 2001 from International Space Station (Expedition 3 crew)",
    "description": "\"The world changed today. What I say or do is very minor compared to the significance of what happened to our country today when it was attacked.\" So said Expedition 3 Commander Frank L. Culbertson, upon learning of the September 11, 2001 attack on the World Trade Center.\nThis image is one of a series taken that day of metropolitan New York City by the International Space Station's Expedition 3 crew that shows a plume of smoke rising from the Manhattan skyline.\n\nUpon further reflection, Commander Culbertson said, \"It's horrible to see smoke pouring from wounds in your own country from such a fantastic vantage point. The dichotomy of being on a spacecraft dedicated to improving life on the earth and watching life being destroyed by such willful, terrible acts is jolting to the psyche, no matter who you are.\"",
    "dateCreated": "2001-09-11",
    "categories": [
      "Aftermath of 9/11 in New York City",
      "Files from NASA with known IDs",
      "ISS Expedition 3 Crew Earth Observations",
      "PD NASA",
      "Satellite pictures of September 11 attacks at the World Trade Center"
    ],
